+# NEXUS — AI Digital Twin for Campus Intelligence
+
+> **"Understand the present. Simulate the future. Prevent the unexpected."**
+
+NEXUS is an AI-powered campus intelligence and prediction platform that creates a
+**continuously updated digital twin** of a college campus. It is **not** an attendance
+or classroom-monitoring system — it is an AI-powered **Campus Command Center** that
+fuses CCTV/video analytics, crowd movement, vehicles, parking, events, weather and
+resource consumption into one live operational picture, then learns normal campus
+patterns, detects anomalies, predicts the future, and simulates "what-if" decisions
+before administrators act in the real world.
+
+```
+Real World → Cameras + Sensors + APIs + Events → AI Data Processing → Digital Twin
+           → Pattern Learning → Anomaly Detection → Future Prediction
+           → What-If Simulation → AI Recommendations
+```
+
+---
+
+## ✨ What NEXUS does
+
+| Capability | Description |
+|---|---|
+| 🏛️ **AI Digital Twin** | Interactive live map of buildings, gates, roads, parking, auditorium, cafeteria, library, sports areas, venues, transport routes and restricted zones — each showing its current state |
+| 📹 **Real-Time Computer Vision** | Person detection, vehicle detection/counting, entry/exit counting, crowd density, restricted-zone and unusual-movement detection from live RTSP or uploaded video — **anonymous, no facial recognition** |
+| 🧠 **Crowd Intelligence** | Crowd size, density (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL), growth rate, concentration and growth prediction per zone |
+| ⚠️ **AI Anomaly Detection** | Learns normal patterns from 30 days of history (per zone, per hour-of-day); flags deviations with z-score/percentile statistics and plain-language explanations |
+| 🔮 **Predictive Intelligence** | Predicts crowd congestion, parking fill-time, traffic buildup, event overcrowding and resource anomalies — always as CURRENT → PREDICTED → RECOMMENDED ACTION |
+| ⭐ **WHAT-IF Simulator** *(signature feature)* | "What happens if the main gate is closed?" / "…if an event attracts 2,000 people?" / "…if Parking Zone A is down?" / "…if heavy rain hits the event?" — simulated against the twin with CURRENT vs SIMULATED comparison charts and AI recommendations |
+| 🎪 **Event Intelligence** | Per-event expected vs current vs predicted peak vs capacity, occupancy and AI risk level; overcrowding-breach prediction |
+| 🅿️ **Smart Parking** | Per-zone occupancy, free slots, fill-time prediction ("Zone A reaches capacity in ~18 minutes"), car/bike mix |
+| 🚌 **Campus Mobility** | Gate/road flow (in/out per minute), congestion levels, movement between zones |
+| ⚡ **Resource Intelligence** | Electricity, water, waste, transport consumption with abnormal-consumption detection |
+| 🌦️ **Environment Intelligence** | Temperature, humidity, rain probability, AQI; weather × outdoor-event disruption risk |
+| 🎯 **AI Risk Engine** | Campus risk score 0–100 (🟢🟡🟠🔴) with weighted contributors (crowd, parking, traffic, events, weather, resources, restricted zones, alerts) |
+| 💬 **AI Decision Assistant** | Natural-language Q&A over live data: "Where is the highest crowd?", "Why is the risk score high?", "What could happen if Gate 1 is closed?" |
+| 🧾 **Explainable AI** | Every risk/alert explains *why* and recommends an action — no black boxes |
+| ⏪ **Campus Event Replay** | Replay Today / Yesterday / Last Week / custom ranges as a time slider over historical snapshots |
+| 📄 **"Explain My Campus"** | AI-generated end-of-day intelligence report (peaks, anomalies, events, risks, summary, recommendations) with export |
+| 🚨 **Smart Alert System** | 10 alert types with location, severity, reason, AI prediction, recommended action, acknowledge/resolve workflow |
+| 📷 **Camera Management** | Camera list with status, AI status, FPS, last update; RTSP/UPLOAD/SIMULATED sources; credentials never exposed to the frontend |
+| 🎬 **Demo Mode** | The **complete system works without CCTV hardware**: 5 simulated cameras (CAM-001…005) generate realistic data; one-click scenario triggers (crowd surge, vehicle surge, parking shortage, gate closure, weather change, resource anomaly, camera offline) |
+| 🔐 **Role-Based Auth** | SUPER_ADMIN / CAMPUS_ADMIN / SECURITY_ADMIN / EVENT_ADMIN, JWT sessions, secure password hashing |
+| 🔒 **Privacy-First** | Anonymous analytics only; facial recognition disabled by design; configurable data retention; access control |
+
+---
+
+## 🏗️ Architecture
+
+```
+┌──────────────┐     ┌───────────────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐
+│  React + TS  │────▶│  FastAPI backend (port 8000)  │◀────│  PostgreSQL     │
+│  Tailwind    │◀────│  • JWT auth + RBAC            │     │  (SQLite demo)  │
+│  Recharts    │ ws  │  • Digital twin engine        │     └─────────────────┘
+│  Campus Map  │────▶│  • Anomaly / prediction /     │     ┌─────────────────┐
+└──────────────┘     │    risk / alert / what-if AI  │◀────│  AI Service     │
+                     │  • WebSocket live updates     │     │  (port 8001)    │
+                     └───────────────────────────────┘     │  OpenCV / YOLO  │
+                                                       │  video analytics│
+                                                       └─────────────────┘
+```
+
+- **AI processing is a separate microservice** (`ai_service/`) — heavy CV work runs in its
+  own process; the backend consumes it over HTTP and falls back to a built-in OpenCV
+  pipeline if the service is unreachable.
+- **Real-time**: the digital twin engine ticks every 3 s and broadcasts the full campus
+  snapshot over WebSockets (`/ws/live`); the frontend also has a polling fallback.
+- **Database**: SQLAlchemy models for Users, Roles, Buildings, Zones, Cameras,
+  CameraEvents, CrowdRecords, VehicleRecords, ParkingZones, ParkingSlots, Events, Alerts,
+  EnvironmentalData, ResourceUsage, TrafficRecords, Predictions, Simulations and
+  CampusMetrics — all timestamped for historical analysis. PostgreSQL in production,
+  SQLite for the local demo.
+
+## 🚀 Quick start
+
+### Option A — Docker (recommended)
+
+```bash
+docker compose up --build
+# Dashboard:  http://localhost        (nginx → frontend)
+# Backend:    http://localhost:8000   (API + docs at /docs)
+# AI service: http://localhost:8001
+```
+
+### Option B — Local development
+
+```bash
+# 1. Backend
+python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt
+cd backend && ../.venv/bin/uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
+
+# 2. AI service (separate process)
+python3 -m venv .venv-ai && .venv-ai/bin/pip install -r ai_service/requirements.txt
+cd ai_service && ../.venv-ai/bin/uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001
+
+# 3. Frontend
+cd frontend && npm install && npm run dev     # http://localhost:5173
+```
+
+The database is seeded automatically on first backend start: demo users, the campus map,
+5 simulated cameras, parking zones, today's events and **30 days of history** that teach
+the anomaly detector what "normal" looks like.
+
+### 🔑 Demo credentials
+
+| User | Role | Password |
+|---|---|---|
+| `superadmin@nexus.ai` | SUPER_ADMIN | `Nexus@2026` |
+| `admin@nexus.ai` | CAMPUS_ADMIN | `Nexus@2026` |
+| `security@nexus.ai` | SECURITY_ADMIN | `Nexus@2026` |
+| `event@nexus.ai` | EVENT_ADMIN | `Nexus@2026` |
+
+## 🎬 Hackathon demo sequence
+
+1. **Log in** as an admin → the dashboard shows the live digital twin.
+2. Observe **normal campus conditions** (risk 🟢/🟡, zones colored by density).
+3. Go to **Settings → Demo Mode** and trigger **EVENT_CROWD** (or CROWD_INCREASE).
+4. Watch the crowd at the venue climb → **AI detects abnormal crowd growth**.
+5. NEXUS **predicts overcrowding** (predicted peak vs capacity) and parking fill-time.
+6. Traffic rises → the **campus risk score** climbs with an explainable breakdown.
+7. **AI recommends actions** (alerts panel, prediction cards, assistant).
+8. Open the **WHAT-IF Simulator** → "What happens if the main gate is closed?"
+9. Run the simulation → compare **REAL CAMPUS vs SIMULATED FUTURE** charts, read the
+   AI-recommended alternative strategy (open Gate 3, redirect ~35% of traffic…).
+10. Open **Explain My Campus** → generate the AI daily intelligence report.
+11. (Optional) **Cameras & CV** → upload any video → person/vehicle counts, crowd
+    density timeline, movement direction.
+
